Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: ask the charger for the status each
 time

The fuel gauge reported the charger's status as cached by its power
supply notifier. When the notifier misses a change, as it does for a
cable pulled while the system sleeps (the cable IRQ is not a wakeup
source and its edge is lost), the battery keeps reporting the old
status: "Full" for the rest of the day after charging to 100 % and
unplugging asleep, while the charger itself says "Discharging".

Read the status from the charger on every request instead and fall
back to the capacity and current based guess only when the charger
doesn't know.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -880,10 +880,15 @@
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
-		/* Get status from charger if available */
+		/*
+		 * Get status from charger if available. Ask it every time:
+		 * a plug event missed in system sleep would leave a cached
+		 * status stale until the next one.
+		 */
 		if (chip->chg_psy &&
-			chip->status != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN) {
-			val->intval = chip->status;
+			!power_supply_get_property(chip->chg_psy,
+				POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS, val) &&
+			val->intval != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN) {
 			break;
 		} else {
 			/*
